      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hey @{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}, it seems section 5B of the privacy policy advises citizens of the EEA, UK and Switzerland that VRChat follows relevant GDPR laws to their country, however it does not advise users on how to request said data.\n\nGoing to https://help.vrchat.com/hc/en-us/requests/new where the typical user is to expect the ability to request their data shows that there is no such relevant option for this.\n\nUnless there is another page in which this data can be requested, I do not believe VRChat adequately complies with article 15 of the GDPR act.\n\nAs lated out under \"The right to obtain\" under this article, the ability to request said documents must be specified in \"laymans terms\" - in which, this is not!\n\nAs such, I do not believe this is complete and is up to spec with this rather crucial part of user privacy and security.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
